{
  "about": "Whole runs, replayed event by event: who may move a run, when, and with what. Each event, in order, is taken or refused; a refused one changes nothing. The first must be control's, from null to pending (not_made otherwise, and for anything before it). A daemon's report must have a from and verify (run/event) with the key the directory (keys) holds for the daemon it names (signature). Then: from must be the run's state now (moved); the move one S37 allows (disallowed); one its reporter may make (reporter): control denied, canceled, expired or failed, an approval approved, a daemon anything but a control_only state; a daemon's report must be about this run from this run's daemon (other_daemon), and its seq the run's next, every event before it counted, control's too (seq); pending straight to running needs the run's standing grant (no_grant). These are the platform's checks (crates/platform/src/db/runs.rs, move_run_in) over arugula_e2e::run, in its order; the detail's own rules there (an exit code, a reason) aren't here.",
